@startuml 04-seq-health-sync
' ============================================================
'  Phase 2 — background health sync.
'  Multi-source ready from day one even though only
'  GoogleHealthApiSource is registered at first.
' ============================================================

title Health Sync — Background Ingestion & Per-Metric Source Resolution (Phase 2)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

participant "WorkManager\n«OS scheduler»" as WM
participant "HealthSyncCoordinator" as Coord
participant "CapabilityRegistry" as CapReg
participant "SourcePriorityResolver" as Priority
participant "GoogleHealthApiSource\n«HealthDataSource»" as Source
participant "TokenStore\nsecure_storage" as Tokens
cloud "Google Health API\nv4" as API
participant "Per-source Mapper\nvendor → canonical" as Mapper
participant "HealthLocalDataSource" as Local
database "Drift / SQLite" as DB
participant "SnapshotResolver" as Resolver
participant "UI\n«via stream»" as UI

== Trigger ==

WM -> Coord : doWork()  «periodic, constraints: network»
activate Coord

Coord -> CapReg : statusFor(all metrics)
activate CapReg
CapReg -> Source : isAvailable()
activate Source
Source --> CapReg : available
deactivate Source
CapReg --> Coord : {steps: ok, hr: ok, sleep: ok, ...}
deactivate CapReg

alt no source available
  Coord -> Coord : record attempt, exit cleanly
  note right of Coord
    Never surfaces a modal.
    UI shows last-known-good
    with a staleness indicator.
  end note
end

Coord -> Priority : orderedSourcesFor(metric)
activate Priority
Priority -> DB : SELECT * FROM source_priority\nWHERE metric = ? ORDER BY rank
activate DB
DB --> Priority : [google_health]
deactivate DB
Priority --> Coord : ranked source list
deactivate Priority

note right of Priority
  One row per metric today.
  Adding Health Connect / HealthKit
  later is a **config change**, not code.
end note

== Fetch cursor ==

Coord -> Local : cursorFor('google_health')
activate Local
Local -> DB : SELECT cursor, consecutive_failures\nFROM sync_cursors
DB --> Local : cursor
Local --> Coord : cursor
deactivate Local

== Authenticated read ==

Coord -> Source : read(from, to, cursor)
activate Source
Source -> Tokens : accessToken()
activate Tokens
Tokens --> Source : token (may be expired)
deactivate Tokens

Source -> API : GET /v4/... (paginated)
activate API

alt 401 Unauthorized
  API --> Source : 401
  Source -> Tokens : refresh()
  activate Tokens
  Tokens -> API : POST token endpoint (refresh_token)
  API --> Tokens : new access + refresh
  Tokens --> Source : new token
  deactivate Tokens
  Source -> API : retry request
end

alt 429 / 5xx
  API --> Source : error
  Source --> Coord : Err(NetworkFailure)
  Coord -> Local : recordFailure('google_health')
  Local -> DB : UPDATE consecutive_failures++,\nnext_attempt = backoff(n)
  note right of Coord #FFF0F0
    Exponential backoff, capped ~6h.
    Never a user-facing error dialog
    for a background sync.
  end note
end

loop while nextPageToken
  API --> Source : page of records
end
deactivate API

Source -> Mapper : normalise(vendorRecords)
activate Mapper
note right of Mapper
  Vendor units, timezone handling,
  sleep-stage taxonomy and session
  enums are converted to the
  **canonical model** here — the only
  place vendor semantics may appear.
end note
Mapper --> Source : List<CanonicalHealthRecord>
deactivate Mapper
Source --> Coord : Ok(records, nextCursor)
deactivate Source

== Persist with DB-enforced dedup ==

loop for each canonical record
  Coord -> Local : upsertSnapshot(record)
  activate Local
  Local -> DB : INSERT ... ON CONFLICT\n(source_id, source_package, source_record_id)\nDO UPDATE
  activate DB
  DB --> Local : ok
  deactivate DB
  deactivate Local
end

note over Local, DB #F0FFF0
  **Dedup is a unique index, not application logic.**
  Re-reading an overlapping window is therefore
  always safe and idempotent.
end note

Coord -> Local : setCursor('google_health', nextCursor)
Local -> DB : UPDATE sync_cursors\n(cursor, last_success_at, failures = 0)

== Resolve winner per metric ==

Coord -> Resolver : resolve(dateRange)
activate Resolver
Resolver -> DB : SELECT * FROM health_snapshots\nWHERE local_date = ?  «one row PER SOURCE»
activate DB
DB --> Resolver : rows (1 today, N later)
deactivate DB
Resolver -> Priority : rank per metric
Resolver -> Resolver : pick highest-ranked source\nwith data for each metric;\nfall through if absent
Resolver -> Resolver : compute coverage\n(days with data / days in window)
Resolver -> DB : write resolved view / materialised row
Resolver --> Coord : resolved
deactivate Resolver

note right of Resolver
  Resolution is **per metric**, not per source:
  best HR from one source, best sleep from
  another, on the same day.
end note

Coord -> Coord : derive HR zones from intraday samples\n+ user max HR, tag zone_model_version
deactivate Coord

DB -->> UI : Drift stream emits → dashboard updates

note over WM, UI #FFFDF0
  **The UI was never blocked and never awaited the network.**
  Sync wrote into Drift; the UI watches Drift.
  This is what makes a future backend additive.
end note

@enduml
